\import{macros}

\title{2026-W45}
\date{2026-11-02}

\p{Start developing math notes on \strong{Formulating Discrete-Induced Physics} ([fdip](https://utensil.github.io/forest/fdip-0001/)): taking the finite structure as the building blocks and the continuum as an emergent large-scale description, on the organizing hypothesis that what continuum analysis does analytically can be recast as algebra on finite-dimensional objects, so that geometry, time, and matter are induced rather than postulated. The aim is to reduce free and unexplained parameters, unlike in the Standard Model: symmetry determines the algebra, written in one unifying geometric-calculus style notation, while the remaining parameters follow from the initial conditions of a specific bubble universe and from the local background. The note suite focuses on mathematical tools that facilitate physical theories, and on worked examples that bridge them. It may supersede the fgap note series, advancing from finite group algebra to a fully discrete setting.}

